{"id": "zh0259", "pool": "zh-causal", "n_q_chunks": 12, "onset_chunk": 11, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "房主要请灭害员上门，更可能的原因是A：他在地下室发现了老鼠。因为灭害员的主要职责就是处理害虫问题，如老鼠、蟑螂等。如果房主发现老鼠在地下室出没，那么他会自然想到请专业人员来处理。而B选项说他在房间里养了一个蚂蚁农场，这通常不需要灭害员帮忙，反而更像是一种爱好或实验，所以房主不会因为这个原因找灭害员上门。", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 40, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "zh0261", "pool": "zh-causal", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The most likely cause of the boy's back pain is that his backpack is heavy. So B, his backpack being heavy, would be the better explanation. While an open backpack might be uncomfortable or distract ing, it wouldn' t typically cause significant back pain. He avy load s on the back, however, can put strain on muscles and lead to discomfort or pain.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 20, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "zh0263", "pool": "zh-causal", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "举重运动员在举过头顶杠铃杆时发出的声音，更可能是他把杠铃杆举过头顶。", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 9, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "zh0265", "pool": "zh-causal", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "我建议我的客人出去吃饭，更可能是因为选项A。我太累了，什么都准备不了。如果只是累到不想做饭，那么让客人去吃饭就很合理了。如果是因为客人逗留过久，通常会说他们待得太久了，而不是主动提议出去吃饭。所以，最可能的原因是我太累了，什么都准备不了。", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "zh0267", "pool": "zh-causal", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "If the power goes out in your house, you're more likely to grab a flash light than a rake. So A is the better answer.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "zh0269", "pool": "zh-causal", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "更可能的原因是 B.我不在城里。这个选项直接说明了你无法参加聚会的具体原因，即地理位置的问题。而A选项虽然可能影响你的情绪，但并不直接解释为什么你拒绝了邀请。所以B更合理。", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 19, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "zh0271", "pool": "zh-causal", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Public speakers often use humor to connect with their audience. So, when a speaker tells a joke, the most likely reaction is laughter from the audience. People usually laugh when they find something funny. Standing up would be unusual unless it was part of an act or a big celebration. So, I think the best answer is A: The audience laughed.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 20, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "zh0273", "pool": "zh-causal", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "They'll win the game. B. The y will lose the game. C. The y will tie the game.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "zh0275", "pool": "zh-causal", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "If your car is overheat ing, the most likely cause would be that the engine has overheated.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 5, "carrier_ended": null}
